        &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5374x3023+0+280/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F47%2Fe2%2F9fe8cd294f2f8e01cfd1568a33db%2Fmagic-school-2-2.jpg" class="img" alt="Lubelo Mthenjana performs a magic trick involving fire during the annual junior magic contest at the College of Magic in Cape Town, South Africa." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Lubelo Mthenjana performs a magic trick involving fire during the annual junior magic contest at the College of Magic in Cape Town, South Africa.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Tommy Trenchard for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Forget flying brooms. Cape Town is home to South Africa's real-world Hogwarts: the College of Magic. Every Saturday, almost 200 students ages 10 to 18 attend classes in a variety of things, including puppetry, mime and clowning, juggling, card tricks, illusions, mentalism, stage magic, theater production and escapology. In 1980, David Gore and a friend came up with the idea of starting a magic school. At the time, South Africa was grappling with apartheid, a brutal system of racial segregation. But from day one, the establishment was multiracial, even though state schools were still strictly segregated. Almost 50 years later, the College of Magic continues to stand out in a city that remains deeply divided along racial and economic lines. These photos capture how the school has turned &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/25/g-s1-149089/magic-magicians-south-africa-school-students" target="_blank"&gt;young dreamers into magicians&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-149586" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 1688;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+115/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F28%2Fe9%2F71f12fec49449d3ca991f500973b%2Fdsc9282.jpg" class="img" alt="A fisherman sorts through a bucket of fish in the late morning light. Invasive blue catfish are a problem in the Chesapeake Bay and its tributaries, preying on native seafood like the blue crab. To help keep them in check, local school children are eating catfish for lunch." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Invasive blue catfish are a problem in the Chesapeake Bay and its tributaries, preying on native seafood like the blue crab. To help keep them in check, local schoolchildren are eating catfish for lunch.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Ryan Kellman/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Blue crabs in the Chesapeake Bay are threatened by invasive blue catfish. To tackle the problem, officials are &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/26/nx-s1-5954211/invasive-blue-catfish-solution-schools-chesapeake-bay" target="_blank"&gt;creating kid-friendly catfish recipes&lt;/a&gt; that meet federal dietary requirements for school lunches in Maryland and Virginia.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Microsoft sent memos yesterday to about 60,000 employees, &lt;a href="https://www.kuow.org/technology/2026-10-26/microsoft-offers-voluntary-buyouts-to-a-quarter-of-its-workforce?utm_source=npr.org&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=national_highlight&amp;utm_content=homepage" target="_blank"&gt;offering voluntary buyouts&lt;/a&gt; to further reduce its headcount. The offer is available to roughly one quarter of its workforce. (via &lt;a href="https://www.kuow.org/" target="_blank"&gt;KUOW&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Archdiocese of New York has agreed to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/24/nx-s1-6015522/new-york-archdiocese-settlement-agreement" target="_blank"&gt;pay $800 million to settle claims&lt;/a&gt; from around 1,300 people who say they faced sexual abuse by clergy members and lay workers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
