ightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1990x1119+70+89/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F22%2F2c%2F747679554efca59d4af9db471a69%2F0tmul-average-prices-of-groceries-over-the-last-six-years.png" class="img" alt="Five charts showing price trends since Jan. 2020 for eggs, ground beef, coffee grounds, butter and chocolate chip cookies" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Trump promised to lower grocery prices in his second term. While some individual items have gotten cheaper since he returned to office, overall grocery prices have risen, driven by factors such as increased labor costs, tariffs and higher energy prices due to the conflict with Iran. Specific issues facing a single crop, animal species or geographic region can cause the price of one item to rise well above inflation, while lowering the price of another. NPR &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/20/nx-s1-5989636/grocery-prices-eggs-coffee-inflation" target="_blank"&gt;analyzed five everyday food items&lt;/a&gt; — ground beef, eggs, coffee, butter and chocolate chip cookies — to better understand the math behind grocery store prices.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag rte2-style-ul"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🍔 Ground beef prices have skyrocketed, reaching $6.79 per pound last month, which is an 85% increase over the past decade, according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics. This surge is largely due to weather and financial pressures on producers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🥚 Prices for eggs fell to $2.27 per dozen last month. Outbreaks like the avian flu can cause significant price fluctuations. In March 2025, the average dozen reached a record high of $6.23.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🧈 In September, a pound of butter averaged $3.96 — down 17.3% from last year. U.S. butter production has surged as dairy farms expanded their herds and boosted milk supply for popular items like Greek yogurt. This has resulted in an oversupply of butter.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🍪 Chocolate chip cookie prices hit a record $5.35 per pound this January, and last month dropped by 20 cents. The price spike is partly due to factors affecting the sweet treat's ingredients, such as higher flour costs driven by the war in Ukraine.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;☕ The U.S. imports 99% of the coffee it consumes. Severe weather and climate change have affected harvests, and the price of coffee is still 44% higher than it was two years earlier, despite Trump removing tariffs on the product.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Read more about &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/20/nx-s1-5989636/grocery-prices-eggs-coffee-inflation" target="_blank"&gt;why these prices have fluctuated here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Weekend picks&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148783" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-so