ot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3600x2024+0+222/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ff4%2F2b%2F298136124d2f94cc25adbc2df627%2Flincoln-piano-1238-c.jpg" class="img" alt="Petter Mattei portrays stars in the Metropolitan Opera production of Lincoln in the Bardo, adapted from George Saunders&amp;#039; surreal novel about the president grieving the loss of his son in the midst of the Civil War." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Petter Mattei portrays stars in the Metropolitan Opera production of &lt;em&gt;Lincoln in the Bardo&lt;/em&gt;, adapted from George Saunders' surreal novel about the president grieving the loss of his son in the midst of the Civil War.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Karen Almond/Metropolitan Opera                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check out what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/culture/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is watching, reading and listening to this weekend:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍿 Movies: &lt;/strong&gt;A new film version of Jane Austen's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/20/nx-s1-6007773/sense-and-sensibility-still-charms-in-a-new-adaptation" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sense and Sensibility&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; focuses on the Dashwood family's two oldest sisters, Elinor and Marianne, who face financial insecurity due to laws that disadvantage widows and daughters.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📺 TV:&lt;/strong&gt; Actor Sharon Horgan stars as Alex, a 50-year-old divorcée who finds herself at multiple personal and professional crossroads in HBO's new show &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/21/nx-s1-6009119/youth-puts-the-mid-in-mid-life" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Youth&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📚 Books:&lt;/strong&gt; Barbara Trapido's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/20/nx-s1-6007701/brother-of-the-more-famous-jack-review" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Brother of the More Famous Jack&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; follows Katherine Browne, who is determined to escape her stiflingly conventional upbringing and create a life with fewer constraints.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎵 Music: &lt;/strong&gt;NPR's &lt;em&gt;New Music Friday&lt;/em&gt; host Stephen Thompson breaks down the best albums released today, including Anderson .Paak and Cordae's &lt;em&gt;Heavy Is the Crown &lt;/em&gt;and Fenne Lily's &lt;em&gt;Win Win&lt;/em&gt;. Listen to a playlist of the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/23/nx-s1-6012325/new-music-friday-the-best-albums-out-oct-23" target="_blank"&gt;best songs from the new albums&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎭 Theater:&lt;/strong&gt; Missy Mazzoli's music brings George Saunders' Booker Prize-winning novel, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/19/nx-s1-6003649/lincoln-bardo-metropolitan-opera-mazzoli-saunders" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lincoln in the Bardo&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, to life in a stage adaptation at the Metropolitan Opera House in New York. Mazzoli is the first woman composer to have a world premiere on the Met stage.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-149281" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3008;         --source-height: 1692;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3008x1692+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F09%2Fee%2F78ce01334929a06e66c660aa1a95%2F2025-turkey.png" class="img" alt="Karl Bushby, pictured here in Turkey in 2025, started his Goliath Expedition 28 years ago." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Karl Bushby, pictured here in Turkey in 2025, started his Goliath Expedition 28 years ago.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Karl Bushby                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag rte2-style-ol"&gt;&lt;li&gt;British adventurer Karl Bushby set out from Chile with the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/21/nx-s1-5998701/karl-bushby-goliath-expedition" target="_blank"&gt;goal of walking an unbroken path&lt;/a&gt; to his hometown in England. After 28 years, he has returned to the U.K. and plans to return to his mother's home in Hull by Nov. 1.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;At least four Trump merchandise stores closed this year as the MAGA Mall reports &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/22/nx-s1-6002970/trump-merchandise-stores-closing-maga-midterms" target="_blank"&gt;sales fell 30%&lt;/a&gt; from his presidential election years.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In this week's edition of Far-Flung Postcards, NPR's Carrie Kahn recalls feeling the rare power of nature at &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/22/g-s1-148553/argentina-brazil-iguazu-falls-waterfalls-super-el-nino" target="_blank"&gt;Iguazú Falls on the Brazil-Argentina border&lt;/a&gt;. A rain-soaked October brought near-record water volumes crashing over the cliffs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
