      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Justice Department has charged 28 green card holders in California with election crimes &lt;/strong&gt;for allegedly illegally registering to vote or voting in U.S. elections. This marks a significant &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/19/nx-s1-6007908/election-tensions-escalate-in-california-as-doj-charges-28-people-with-voting-crimes" target="_blank"&gt;escalation in the Trump administration's feud&lt;/a&gt; with the state over its voting system as the midterm elections approach. The DOJ also filed an emergency request to prevent California from processing ballots returned by people on the voter rolls that the federal government says are "likely noncitizens." California has sought clarification on the federal government's conclusions but has not received any. Last week, the DOJ sued California and Los Angeles County after local officials refused to investigate allegations made by the administration about noncitizen voting.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148846" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4800;         --source-height: 2700;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4800x2700+0+88/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F94%2F07%2F5a6e97054f21a7963d525f678dfd%2Fgettyimages-2278611370.jpg" class="img" alt="People vote in Norwalk, Calif., during early voting in California&amp;#039;s primary election on June 1, 2026. The Department of Justice has charged 28 green card holders in the state for allegedly illegally registering to vote or voting in U.S. elections, in an escalation of a feud with California officials over the state’s voting system." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 People vote in Norwalk, Calif., during early voting in California's primary election on June 1, 2026. The Department of Justice has charged 28 green card holders in the state for allegedly illegally registering to vote or voting in U.S. elections, in an escalation of a feud with California officials over the state's voting system.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Frederic J. Brown/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧&lt;strong&gt; The DOJ wants California to segregate ballots of those on its list&lt;/strong&gt; and to delay counting them until investigations are complete. Election law experts &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6008838:x" target="_blank"&gt;doubt the DOJ will succeed&lt;/a&gt;, given its past attempts to change state voting processes, Miles Parks tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt;. He adds that it would be surprising to see a shift just two weeks before the election with ballots already distributed. Research shows that in many cases, when legal permanent residents register to vote, it is due to a misunderstanding of the rules. Experts tell Parks they are concerned that federal law enforcement might use accusations to confiscate ballots during counting, but many local voting officials are preparing by keeping county attorneys on speed dial.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Democrats and Republicans are deciding which races to prioritize&lt;/strong&gt; with Election Day just two weeks away. President Trump is campaigning in key perennial purple states like Georgia, North Carolina, Kansas, Iowa and Florida this week.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;Trump's rally in Kansas and trip to North Carolina aren't where&lt;/strong&gt; the leader of the Republican Party's attention should be, NPR's Stephen Fowler says. Kansas hasn't elected a Democratic senator in nearly a century, and many Republican groups have ceased ad spending in North Carolina, viewing the Senate race as a lost cause. Republicans are prioritizing &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6008838:x" target="_blank"&gt;efforts to save their Senate majority&lt;/a&gt; over saving the House majority, while Democrats are capitalizing on opportunities in conservative areas, Fowler says. In Georgia, with a million voters already casting ballots, Fowler says he sees an increase in Black voter turnout in the state and across the South.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ &lt;strong&gt;The NPR App has all of NPR's election coverage in one place&lt;/strong&gt; — from the biggest stories across the country, to the issues that matter close to home. Browse headlines, playlists, podcast episodes, videos and more, all on the &lt;a href="https://npr.app/stqe/election-2026" target="_blank"&gt;2026 Election tab&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TikTok employees repeatedly raised concerns about the app's risks to children&lt;/strong&gt;, including sexual exploitation and exposure to suicide content. Previously unreported court records show employees' frustration with leadership's response to these issues. Depositions filed in March 2026 provide new insights into TikTok's child safety measures since its surge in popularity in 2018. Staff alerted management about minors engaging with sexual content, which the &lt;a href="http://www.npr.org/2026/10/20/nx-s1-6005809/tiktok-child-safety-money-laundering" target="_blank"&gt;company profited from&lt;/a&gt;. They also identified loopholes that allowed users under 18 to bypass age restrictions and block parental oversight of their app activity. The records show that TikTok avoided conducting age surveys, fearing it would have to share results with the Federal Trade Commission.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Life advice&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148644" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2048;         --source-height: 1152;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2048x1152+0+448/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F07%2Fa8%2F51f0573d483da4b36993cac419e8%2Fcold-and-flu.jpg" class="img" alt="Cold and flu kit items " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Cold and flu season in the U.S. starts this month and lasts through May, according ot the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Cooler temperatures and drier air can increase our vulnerability to illnesses like the common cold, flu, RSV and COVID-19. Get ahead of the game now by putting together a cold-and-flu prep kit. Here's what &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/15/nx-s1-6001703/essential-items-to-stock-in-your-medicine-cabinet-for-cold-and-flu-season" target="_blank"&gt;experts say you should have in your home&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🤒 Over-the-counter medications are good options, but always follow the recommended dosage to avoid risks or side effects. Some good medications to have include ibuprofen or naproxen, which can relieve headaches, body aches and sore throats by reducing inflammation and Acetaminophen, which can lower body temperature.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🤒 Honey acts as an anti-inflammatory and soothes the throat, making it useful for young children who can't take cough medicine. But don't give it to children under 12 months due to the risk of botulism.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🤒 A thermometer is a must-have for checking your temperature. For children 3 and under, a rectal option is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🤒 A saline spray or rinse for your nose can help keep the mucous membranes moist and help relieve symptoms by loosening thick mucus during a cold.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;For more advice on how to stock your medicine cabinet for cold and flu season, &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5996845:x" target="_blank"&gt;listen to this episode of NPR's &lt;em&gt;Life Kit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Subscribe to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/life-kit" target="_blank"&gt;the &lt;em&gt;Life Kit&lt;/em&gt; newsletter&lt;/a&gt; for expert advice on love, money, relationships and more.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Picture show&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148423" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4000;         --source-height: 2249;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2249+239+663/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F78%2Fc5%2Feecbf8f0401f8e9d220536fbdd3c%2Flannaapisukh-npr-americangirl-5085.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2249+239+663/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F78%2Fc5%2Feecbf8f0401f8e9d220536fbdd3c%2Flannaapisukh-npr-americangirl-5085.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2249+239+663/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F78%2Fc5%2Feecbf8f0401f8e9d220536fbdd3c%2Flannaapisukh-npr-americangirl-5085.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2249+239+663/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F78%2Fc5%2Feecbf8f0401f8e9d220536fbdd3c%2Flannaapisukh-npr-americangirl-5085.jpg 900w, https:/